    <statement><p>Are the functions below polynomials?  If they are, enter their degree.  If not, enter <em>NONE.</em></p>
<p><m>f(x) = 6^x + 4</m> has degree <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>g(x) = x^{6} + 4</m> has degree <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{NONE}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



<m>f(x)</m> is not a polynomial because the term <m>6^x</m> is exponential, not polynomial.



<m>g(x)</m> is a polynomial of degree 6, since the highest power of <m>x</m> is <m>x^6</m>.



</solution>
